SNEEZING. recently tends in the direction of sneezing. This being so it behaves the sneezer to select the right day on which to perform this sometimes agreeable function. An old rhyme has it:—
Sneeze on a Monday,
You get a letter;
Sneeze on a Tuesday,
You get something better;
Sneeze on a Wednesday,
You sneeze for danger;
Sneeze on a Thursday;
Meet a stranger;
Sneeze on a Friday.
Sneeze for sorrow;
Sneeze on a Saturday;
See your best friend to morrow.
